==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|m|u}}

===Etymology===
From Common Germanic *''[[murthaz]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*Hyphenation: mur·ha
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:Finnish:-urhɑ|-urhɑ]]
*{{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈmurhɑ]}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun|murh|type=koira}}

# [[murder|Murder]].
# {{law|lang=fi}} [[murder|Murder]], [[homicide]] (''premeditated and/or more brutal, and, therefore, more aggravated than [[tappo]]'').

====Usage notes====
*(''law:'') The order of homicidal crimes &mdash;by how severe they are considered in Finnish law&mdash; is (from the least aggravated to the most aggravated) [[kuolemantuottamus]] ("involuntary manslaughter") -> [[surma]] ("voluntary manslaughter under mitigating circumstances") -> [[tappo]] ("voluntary manslaughter" or "homicide", under no mitigating circumstances) -> [[murha]] ("murder", "homicide", killing of a person by another under aggravating circumstances, premeditated and/or brutal).

